{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And we have become.</b> ועתה היינו כטמא כולנו." "<b>Like one who slaughters [ prey ].</b> Like יאכל עד (Genesis 49:27), for the garment of spoil is stained with blood. [n: The lemma עדים is resolved as עד 'prey/plunder' per the comparison to Genesis 49:27; Ibn Ezra reads it as related to spoil stained with blood.]" "<b>And we fade.</b> To join the nun of the root, for it is from the paradigm of נובלת עליה (Isaiah 1:30), with the nun of the speaking-sign [i.e., first-person prefix] lacking the nun of the root, and אפס on its pattern. [n: The last phrase 'ואפס על משקלו' is obscure; translated hyper-literally. Possibly 'and there is none like its pattern' or 'and אפס follows its pattern,' the reference is uncertain.]"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 64, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:00:57.180062071Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}